{%- comment -%}
  One photograph of the product page gallery. main-product decides everything
  about it (its label, its alt, whether it is on screen) and this only draws
  it, so image 1 of the set, which is drawn after the loop, and the rest can
  never drift apart.

  Accepts:
  - media {Object} the image
  - index {Number} its position among the product's images, from 1. The page
    arrives with image 1 of the set moved to the top of the gallery, so the
    script needs this to put the rest back in product order after a switch.
  - label {String} the option value it belongs to, lower-cased; blank = shared
  - alt {String} the composed alt ("Product — Black")
  - hidden {Boolean} off screen for the variant being shown
  - sizes {String} the column's sizes attribute
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="pdp-gallery__item"
  data-gallery-item
  data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
  data-media-index="{{ index }}"
  {% if label != blank %}
    data-variant-label="{{ label | escape }}"
  {% endif %}
  {% if hidden %}
    hidden
  {% endif %}
>
  {{-
    media
    | image_url: width: 2400
    | image_tag:
      widths: '550, 750, 1100, 1500, 2000, 2400',
      sizes: sizes,
      loading: 'lazy',
      alt: alt
  -}}
</div>
